from pathlib import Path
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent/'stage/d7c9faad43d9/astraupskill'
extra={
'README.md':'''Use this project to distinguish request shape from relationship validity. A positive integer passes the route schema even when no corresponding city exists. The store guard closes that gap for direct callers as well as the admin UI. The expanded four-case lab also preserves existing rows, checks actual text/list normalization, propagates write failure and documents duplicate-name behavior. Begin with a prediction, inspect the before snapshot, then run the tests. Finish by explaining why reading a JSON file and later rewriting it is not equivalent to a database transaction.''',
'01-CODEBASE-MAP.md':'''Read the POST handler carefully: it returns 201 only after creation succeeds, and maps caught errors to 400 with a message. The store throws a plain Error; it does not choose an HTTP status itself. The wrapper passes normalized optional fields through to the store. Within readStore, ensureStoreFile calls mkdir before reading, so rejected creation still may perform directory setup. The zero-write assertion specifically means no writeFile call. Follow the successful return object back through the wrapper to the response, marking which layers are only source-reviewed and which the VM actually executes.''',
'02-CONCEPTS.md':'''Call this parent existence or referential integrity, not user ownership: city membership does not authorize an actor. Authentication remains in the admin request helper, which the focused tests do not run. Likewise, a parent check does not enforce unique shop names. Repeating a valid create allocates another id with the same slug under the current policy. A future uniqueness rule needs its own contract and concurrency design. The same-file parent lookup provides a useful single-operation check, but another process could still modify the file between read and write.''',
'03-WORKED-CHANGE.md':'''The accepted positive fixture starts with shop id nine, so the next id must be ten. Existing rows and cities must survive serialization unchanged. Name whitespace is trimmed, an empty address becomes null, duplicate specialties collapse and publication remains false. Actual utility functions execute for text and array cleanup; slugify itself is an explicit adapter, so only its options and propagation are asserted. This distinction prevents a passing test from claiming coverage of a third-party algorithm it never loaded. The source patch remains the small parent guard; broader tests protect the surrounding valid behavior.''',
'04-TESTING-AND-DEBUGGING.md':'''The four accepted cases use fresh serialized fixtures. The negative matrix includes an unknown numeric id and a string containing the valid number, demonstrating strict comparison at the store boundary. A write-error case preserves error identity and records one attempted write, while a repeated-create case checks ids ten and eleven. The fixture's write adapter throws before saving bytes; real filesystem failures can behave differently. Do not infer atomic writes or rollback from that test. Debug the first mismatch in returned payload, serialized bytes or call count rather than assuming every failed assertion points at the city guard.''',
'05-PRACTICE.md':'''Use two points each for relationship validation, valid normalization, preservation of existing rows, error propagation and limits. Predict the result for cityId 7 versus the string "7" when calling the store directly, then compare this with the route's numeric schema. For mutation practice, remove the guard and observe the rejected-call assertion fail. For design practice, draw two processes that read the same highest id before either writes; explain what can be lost. Propose a database constraint or serialized write mechanism as future work without claiming the current patch implements it.''',
'06-SOLUTIONS-AND-REVIEW.md':'''Starting from id nine, valid creates return ten and then eleven; duplicate names are still allowed. City 999 and string "7" fail the strict predicate without writeFile calls. The actual text utility turns a whitespace-only address into null and deduplicates trimmed specialties. A disk adapter rejection returns no successful shop to the caller and preserves the original error. The route's existing catch would map an Error message to 400, but that handler was not executed. Full review credit requires separating parent integrity, authentication, normalization, uniqueness and persistence guarantees rather than treating them as one generic validation feature.''',
'07-TRACE-LAB.md':'''Use this worksheet to separate attempts from durable effects:

| Input | Read and directory setup | Guard | writeFile |
|---|---|---|---|
| Valid city | Attempted | Pass | Once |
| Unknown city | Attempted | Throw | Never |
| String city id | Attempted | Throw | Never |
| Valid city, write fails | Attempted | Pass | One failed attempt |

An in-memory push before a later throw does not necessarily change the saved JSON, because readStore parsed a fresh object. Therefore a zero-write assertion cannot detect every temporary object mutation. Inspect source placement as well as observable I/O; the accepted guard precedes both construction and push.''',
'VERIFICATION.md':'''The accepted label crud-b04-astra-runtime has four passing cases. Actual store and utility modules execute, while filesystem, path, slugify, clsx, scoring and research-schema dependencies are adapters. Nullable-text and array cleanup are real; third-party slug generation is not. The local Next.js documentation directory was absent after dependency cleanup, and no framework API was changed. The write-failure case verifies rejection with the original error, not preservation under a real partial disk write. All failed attempts remain in workspace evidence; accepted logs and exact command are linked below after review.'''
}
